+      "description": "s234-D5 (Dave, #234) + s245-D1 (grammar (a), #245): `behaviour` promoted from optional prose notes to a TYPED OBJECT carrying the script/partial ADDRESS. The meta is the ONE HOME (s234-D4/D5: generation chain, never copy chain): gen_component_partials.py DERIVES a #behaviour-manifest block into the snippet beside #token-manifest, and _validate_receipt.py reads THIS object to check that a composed page loads what the meta declares. `script` GRAMMAR — three forms, nothing else resolves: null = the component carries NO script (a POSITIVE declaration, never 'unknown'); `knowledge/<path>.js` = a hand-authored source file, the component-types.json $behaviour form (e.g. knowledge/canon/dv-behaviour.js); `knowledge/snippets/<Slug>.reference.html#script` = the snippet's own inline executable <script> element(s) outside any AUTO-BEHAVIOUR markers. `partial` = the AUTO-BEHAVIOUR name(s) registered under component-types.json $behaviour that the snippet carries — one name, a list of names (s245-D2: 9 of the 14 dataviz members carry 2-3), else null. `events` = DOM event names as passed to addEventListener — s245-D4: KEPT, OPTIONAL, generated from the snippet, never authored (rC Q3 answered). `fallback` = what the component does with CSS on and JS off (rA resilience criterion, GOV.UK/USWDS); null = NOT DECLARED (an honest UNPROVEN), never 'none' — a passive component says so in words ('identical — the component carries no script'). `$note` keeps the pre-s234-D5 prose VERBATIM (by-addition migration, ADR-0017 archive-never-delete). `$unproven` names the fields whose value is null because neither the prose nor a probe settles them. Existence of the addressed file/script is NOT a schema question — the generator and the gate resolve it (gate the presence, not the shape).",
+      "type": "object",
+      "required": [
+        "script",
+        "partial",
+        "fallback"
+      ],
+      "additionalProperties": false,
+      "patternProperties": {
